1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,626
Pactra explores agentic payments: how can several delegated workers share one
spending limit?

2
00:00:04,626 --> 00:00:12,100
This demo connects a local test wallet, signs real contract transactions, and
shows a looping worker stopped by a budget rule.

3
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:15,529
First, connect the local test wallet.

4
00:00:15,529 --> 00:00:19,245
I review the twenty dollar mandate and confirm its transaction.

5
00:00:19,245 --> 00:00:23,333
Funding needs two signatures: a token approval, then the vault deposit.

6
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:25,934
I then sign three narrower worker mandates.

7
00:00:25,934 --> 00:00:30,021
These are real browser-signed transactions on isolated Anvil, using mock
funds.

8
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:34,749
The owner console reads the signed mandate directly from the contracts.

9
00:00:34,749 --> 00:00:38,278
The root has a twenty dollar window budget and three workers.

10
00:00:38,278 --> 00:00:42,770
Two accepted draws total seventy seven cents, charged to their workers and the
root.

11
00:00:42,770 --> 00:00:44,374
These are actual contract reads.

12
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:48,243
The tree shows how authority is shared.

13
00:00:48,243 --> 00:00:52,062
Every accepted draw charges its own node and all ancestors.

14
00:00:52,062 --> 00:00:54,735
Children can only narrow the parent policy.

15
00:00:54,735 --> 00:00:58,936
Tranche, window, lifetime, revocation and declared counterparty rules
constrain each draw.

16
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:02,252
The product walkthrough explains a purchase.

17
00:01:02,252 --> 00:01:05,773
An agent asks for a URL through the payment runtime.

18
00:01:05,773 --> 00:01:09,294
The seller returns an x four oh two price challenge.

19
00:01:09,294 --> 00:01:12,815
Pactra checks the mandate path and obtains bounded payment capacity.

20
00:01:12,815 --> 00:01:13,871
Settlement happens afterwards.

21
00:01:13,871 --> 00:01:16,687
Agent-facing tools do not receive the operator key.

22
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:24,157
Now the local harness submits seven requests of fifty one cents from one
worker to the same declared seller.

23
00:01:24,157 --> 00:01:27,125
Six are accepted, totaling three dollars and six cents.

24
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:30,753
The seventh would exceed that worker's three dollar fifty concentration
allowance.

25
00:01:30,753 --> 00:01:32,072
The contract refuses it.

26
00:01:32,072 --> 00:01:37,020
The root now records three dollars and eighty three cents, including the
earlier useful work.

27
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:43,097
The refusals view shows the actual rejected request, its amount, and the
concentration reason.

28
00:01:43,097 --> 00:01:45,884
Refused draws do not consume the agent budget.

29
00:01:45,884 --> 00:01:51,458
Owner administration is a separate trust boundary: an explicit owner release
can bypass agent budget accounting.

30
00:01:51,458 --> 00:01:56,335
This prototype does not remove the need to trust the owner or payment runtime.

31
00:01:57,530 --> 00:02:02,901
An AI orchestrator integrates through three MCP tools: fetch, spawn, and
status.

32
00:02:02,901 --> 00:02:07,824
It can request paid resources, delegate narrower authority, and inspect
headroom.

33
00:02:07,824 --> 00:02:12,300
The repository includes the contracts, payment runtime, console, and
evaluation.

34
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:17,671
Stress experiments use scripted workers, not a claim of general AI
reliability.

35
00:02:18,870 --> 00:02:25,624
In the recorded looping-worker comparison, Pactra completed all three tasks
with nine dollars and eighteen cents of loop spending.

36
00:02:25,624 --> 00:02:31,668
Independent wallets also completed all three, with twenty seven dollars and
fifty four cents of loop spending.

37
00:02:31,668 --> 00:02:33,445
The shared cap completed none.

38
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:37,711
These are controlled local results with mock settlement, not production
payment metrics.

39
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:42,845
The focus is bounded autonomy, observable failures, and reproducible evidence.

40
00:02:42,845 --> 00:02:48,747
The archive reports one hundred and one contract cases, and ten evaluation
tests passed again.

41
00:02:48,747 --> 00:02:52,682
This is a prototype, without professional audit or formal verification.

42
00:02:52,682 --> 00:02:56,224
Explore the code and reproduce the demonstration from GitHub.
